{"parentUuid":"2249667e-3315-4784-a588-30302ad38d7a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae1c7e820d9066234","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CeZLMeVY8MtrqYJ8QwrD7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XWCXCh9KHtaRzDVbrfCjWY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom build.operators import laplacian_eigenvalues, linear_operator, K_defect, J_defect\nimport numpy as np\n\n# R0 at N=24\neigs = laplacian_eigenvalues('R0', 24)\nprint(f'R0 N=24: {len(eigs)} modes, eigs range [{eigs.min()}, {eigs.max()}]')\n\nL = linear_operator('R0', 24)\nprint(f'L shape: {L.shape}, K={K_defect(L):.2e}, J={J_defect(L):.2e}')\n\"","description":"Test operators.py with the provided test script","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1632,"cache_read_input_tokens":38623,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1632,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeZLMdgfPtbuLrVv2RDCj","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d50213c-c4d6-4b6b-9e7e-37951a608898","timestamp":"2026-08-30T17:33:54.425Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/blake/Desktop/MIT/OpenWave/M8.5C2_BUILD","sessionId":"df404d7f-30da-41ec-8c3e-12ef3f92c53b","version":"2.1.251","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-orbiting-pelican"}
{"parentUuid":"6d50213c-c4d6-4b6b-9e7e-37951a608898","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e22f4082-815d-4291-8ec0-471a24337109","agentId":"ae1c7e820d9066234","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XWCXCh9KHtaRzDVbrfCjWY","type":"tool_result","content":"R0 N=24: 60 modes, eigs range [0.0, 624.0]\nL shape: (60, 60), K=0.00e+00, J=0.00e+00","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"154485a0-eae2-4cf5-89f2-c8091dafedfe","timestamp":"2026-08-30T17:33:59.416Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"R0 N=24: 60 modes, eigs range [0.0, 624.0]\nL shape: (60, 60), K=0.00e+00, J=0.00e+00","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6d50213c-c4d6-4b6b-9e7e-37951a608898","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/blake/Desktop/MIT/OpenWave/M8.5C2_BUILD","sessionId":"df404d7f-30da-41ec-8c3e-12ef3f92c53b","version":"2.1.251","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-orbiting-pelican"}
{"parentUuid":"154485a0-eae2-4cf5-89f2-c8091dafedfe","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae1c7e820d9066234","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CeZLNagchS4fGRtWo4o3k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Let me also verify the Jacobian works correctly by running a quick sanity check similar to the pattern in `jacobian_check.py`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_read_input_tokens":40255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":352,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeZLNYbbxBL3CYYBa5CT5","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"75c60786-4c31-40d1-8515-8b7b7eca0629","timestamp":"2026-08-30T17:34:04.078Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/blake/Desktop/MIT/OpenWave/M8.5C2_BUILD","sessionId":"df404d7f-30da-41ec-8c3e-12ef3f92c53b","version":"2.1.251","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-orbiting-pelican"}
{"parentUuid":"75c60786-4c31-40d1-8515-8b7b7eca0629","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae1c7e820d9066234","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CeZLNagchS4fGRtWo4o3k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RKoYbuCp2gZ18AwjTWtkps","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom build.operators import laplacian_eigenvalues, linear_operator, real_jacobian, K_defect, J_defect\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Quick Jacobian sanity check: finite-difference comparison\nrho, N = 'R0', 12\nm = 60  # we'll use whatever total_modes gives\nfrom build.sections import total_modes\nm = total_modes(rho, N)\nprint(f'{rho} N={N}: m={m} complex modes, Jacobian is {2*m}x{2*m}')\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(42)\nphi = rng.normal(size=m) + 1j * rng.normal(size=m)\nphi /= np.linalg.norm(phi)\nomega = 2.0\nc1 = 1.0\n\nJ = real_jacobian(phi, omega, rho, N, c1=c1)\nprint(f'J shape: {J.shape}')\nprint(f'J is symmetric (K_defect): {K_defect(J):.2e}')\nprint(f'J imaginary spectrum (J_defect): {J_defect(J):.2e}')\n\n# Finite-difference check\ndef R_res(phi_c, om, eigs, c1):\n    l = -eigs\n    return l * phi_c - c1 * np.vdot(phi_c, phi_c).real * phi_c + om**2 * phi_c\n\ndef real_vec(z): return np.concatenate([z.real, z.imag])\ndef cplx_vec(x): return x[:len(x)//2] + 1j * x[len(x)//2:]\n\neigs = laplacian_eigenvalues(rho, N)\nJ_fd = np.zeros((2*m, 2*m))\nh = 1e-7\nv0 = real_vec(phi)\nfor k in range(2*m):\n    e = np.zeros(2*m); e[k] = h\n    J_fd[:, k] = (real_vec(R_res(cplx_vec(v0 + e), omega, eigs, c1))\n                  - real_vec(R_res(cplx_vec(v0 - e), omega, eigs, c1))) / (2*h)\n\nerr = np.linalg.norm(J - J_fd) / np.linalg.norm(J_fd)\nprint(f'||J_analytic - J_fd|| / ||J_fd|| = {err:.2e}')\n\n# Check gauge mode: i*phi should be in kernel at a solution\nnrm2 = np.vdot(phi, phi).real\n# Not at a solution, so gauge check won't be zero. Just verify FD agreement.\nprint('Jacobian finite-difference agreement: ' + ('PASS' if err < 1e-6 else 'FAIL'))\n\"","description":"Verify Jacobian against finite differences","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_read_input_tokens":40255,"output_tokens":869,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":352},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":869,"cache_read_input_tokens":40255,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":352,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeZLNYbbxBL3CYYBa5CT5","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"81fc1e0e-0907-43eb-8a4d-bda06cfc58f0","timestamp":"2026-08-30T17:34:17.372Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/blake/Desktop/MIT/OpenWave/M8.5C2_BUILD","sessionId":"df404d7f-30da-41ec-8c3e-12ef3f92c53b","version":"2.1.251","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-orbiting-pelican"}
{"parentUuid":"81fc1e0e-0907-43eb-8a4d-bda06cfc58f0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e22f4082-815d-4291-8ec0-471a24337109","agentId":"ae1c7e820d9066234","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RKoYbuCp2gZ18AwjTWtkps","type":"tool_result","content":"R0 N=12: m=14 complex modes, Jacobian is 28x28\nJ shape: (28, 28)\nJ is symmetric (K_defect): 0.00e+00\nJ imaginary spectrum (J_defect): 0.00e+00\n||J_analytic - J_fd|| / ||J_fd|| = 4.36e-10\nJacobian finite-difference agreement: PASS","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6170ecf3-5efa-49e9-a539-0ad9c67bb4db","timestamp":"2026-08-30T17:34:19.969Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"R0 N=12: m=14 complex modes, Jacobian is 28x28\nJ shape: (28, 28)\nJ is symmetric (K_defect): 0.00e+00\nJ imaginary spectrum (J_defect): 0.00e+00\n||J_analytic - J_fd|| / ||J_fd|| = 4.36e-10\nJacobian finite-difference agreement: PASS","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"81fc1e0e-0907-43eb-8a4d-bda06cfc58f0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/blake/Desktop/MIT/OpenWave/M8.5C2_BUILD","sessionId":"df404d7f-30da-41ec-8c3e-12ef3f92c53b","version":"2.1.251","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-orbiting-pelican"}
{"parentUuid":"6170ecf3-5efa-49e9-a539-0ad9c67bb4db","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae1c7e820d9066234","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CeZLQ2Vff7q3j8sQ8k5PF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything checks out. Here is a summary of what was built:\n\n**File created:** `/Users/blake/Desktop/MIT/OpenWave/M8.5C2_BUILD/build/operators.py`\n\n**Functions provided:**\n\n1. **`laplacian_eigenvalues(rho, N)`** -- Returns a 1-D float array of length `total_modes(rho, N)` where each entry holds `n(n+2)` for the level `n` that basis function belongs to. Level-major ordering (intertwiner-index, then multiplet-index within each level).\n\n2. **`linear_operator(rho, N)`** -- Returns the diagonal Laplacian matrix `diag(-n(n+2))` of shape `(m, m)` where `m = total_modes(rho, N)`.\n\n3. **`real_jacobian(phi, omega, rho, N, c1=1.0)`** -- Assembles the `2m x 2m` real Jacobian of `R(phi; omega) = Delta phi - c1 <phi,phi> phi + omega^2 phi`. The formula is `J = diag([l; l]) + omega^2 I - c1 ||phi||^2 I - 2 c1 v v^T` where `l` is the Laplacian diagonal and `v = [Re(phi); Im(phi)]`. This correctly handles the non-holomorphic `<phi,phi> phi` term (rank-1 real update, not a complex Jacobian).\n\n4. **`K_defect(A)`** -- Self-adjointness defect `||A - A^H||_2`.\n\n5. **`J_defect(A)`** -- Imaginary spectrum defect `max |Im lambda(A)|`.\n\n**Test results:**\n- R0 at N=24: 60 modes, eigenvalues range [0, 624], L is 60x60, K=0, J=0 (as expected for a real diagonal matrix).\n- Jacobian verified against central finite differences: relative error 4.36e-10 (PASS). The Jacobian is exactly symmetric (`K_defect = 0`) with purely real spectrum (`J_defect = 0`), consistent with the cubic residual being the gradient of a real functional."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":977,"cache_read_input_tokens":40642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":977,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeZLQ1h3txpGU8ouBpafJ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ec86c324-b3fa-4a48-9d31-d4abe24e0aad","timestamp":"2026-08-30T17:34:35.226Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/blake/Desktop/MIT/OpenWave/M8.5C2_BUILD","sessionId":"df404d7f-30da-41ec-8c3e-12ef3f92c53b","version":"2.1.251","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-orbiting-pelican"}
